%9Setting:%9

    resize_debug (boolean; default: OFF)

%9Description:%9

    Writes a debug log of every terminal resize: the new size, how the
    main windows and the side panels are laid out again and each redraw,
    with times. For tracking down a terminal that is drawn wrong after a
    resize; leave it off otherwise.

    The log is in the erssi home (~/.erssi unless erssi was started with
    --home), named after the terminal:

        resize-<TERM>-<terminal>-<multiplexer>.log

    for example resize-xterm-256color-kitty-tmux.log. It starts with the
    terminal's environment (TERM, COLORTERM, TERM_PROGRAM and the like)
    and is readable only by you. A link or anything but a file of your own
    in its place is not written to. ON opens the log at once and appends
    to it, OFF closes it.

%9Examples:%9

    /SET resize_debug on
    /SET resize_debug off

%9See also:%9

    SET, RESIZE, SIDEPANEL_DEBUG

